\section{Conclusion}
TriVLA presents a novel triple-system architecture that effectively integrates vision-language understanding with dynamic perception, enhancing the robot’s capability to capture both static and future dynamic information. This integration enables more fluid and generalized control policies for robot manipulation. Experimental results demonstrate that TriVLA outperforms state-of-the-art imitation learning baselines on standard simulation benchmarks and challenging real-world tasks, highlighting its potential for broad applications in general robotic control.

