A single node features 384 GB of memory, where
the sum of L2 and L3 caches amounts to 305 MB, which
corresponds to $\approx38 \times 10^6$ floating point double-precision numbers.
The full width of the AVX-512 instruction set (8
double-precision or 16 single-precision floating point numbers) is used in a
vectorization-across-cells strategy~\cite{KronbichlerKormann2019}. The
GNU compiler version 13.2.0 with flags ``-O3 -march=native'' and 
