However, learning shared features may be useless when there is a strong imbalance in how each modality correlates with precipitation.
In contrast, we find that knowledge distillation (KD)\cite{mmanet, prototype, mlim} offers a more feasible solution. 
%It transfers precipitation-related knowledge from the teacher model that uses all modalities to the student model that may only have IR data, facilitating more effective learning with missing modalities.
It transfers precipitation-related knowledge from high-quality multimodal data to low-quality IR data through a teacher-student model, facilitating more effective learning with missing modalities.
Despite this, transferring knowledge is challenging, especially because IR data’s broader coverage doesn’t necessarily translate to more useful knowledge about precipitation.
