\subsection{Overview of PRE-Net and Multimodal Knowledge Expansion}
%PRE-Net is a novel framework designed to address the PRE task, enabling accurate infrared-based full-disc precipitation retrieval. 
%The overall multimodal knowledge expansion pipeline is illustrated in Fig.~\ref{fig:fig2}. PRE-Net is a U-shaped model that incorporates specialized Coordinated Masking and Wavelet Enhancement (CoMWE) modules on the encoder side, as described in Stage I.
The Multimodal Knowledge Expansion (MKE) pipeline is illustrated in Fig.\ref{fig:fig2}.
PRE-Net is a U-shape model that incorporates specialized Coordinated Masking and Wavelet Enhancement (CoMWE) modules on the encoder side, 
which enables PRE-Net to encode richer and more detailed features. 
Overall, the MKE pipeline consists of the Swath-Distilling and Full-Disc Adaptation stages. In Stage I, we pre-train a multimodal UNet model that integrates various swath data, including $X_{IR}, X_ {PMW}, X_ {PR}$, to learn joint feature representations for precipitation retrieval. This pre-trained model then serves as a multimodal teacher, transferring its knowledge to a single-modal PRE-Net, which performs precipitation retrieval using only swath IR data.
%In Stage I, IR data is encoded by several CoMWEs and aligned with the teacher's features via distillation. 
%In Stage II, the single-modal PRE-Net employs Self-MaskTune to adaptively generate masks, adapting the model for full-disc infrared data and refining the its predictions. 
In Stage II, the single-modal PRE-Net undergoes Full-Disc Adaptation, where we employ LoRA~\cite{lora} and Self-MaskTune to refine its ability to perform full-disc precipitation retrieval while keeping the knowledge transferred from the teacher model to handle the broader spatial coverage provided by IR data.
%In the second stage, Full-Disc Adaptation adapts the model for full-disc infrared data by employing Self-MaskTune to balance multimodal and infrared-specific knowledge. 
%This staged pipeline synergizes robust multimodal learning with effective single-modality generalization, yielding high-quality precipitation retrieval.
The two-stage pipeline enables PRE-Net to bridge the gap between multimodal data integration and effective single-modality generalization, enhancing the accuracy and robustness of precipitation retrieval.
As a result, PRE-Net can achieve high-quality full-disc retrieval relying solely on IR data.
