\textbf{Informal resource-based approaches} also rely on external resources, but instead of formal resources like ontologies, they utilize informal resources such as annotated relationships between entities or text. A prevalent method involves employing a thesaurus such as thesaurus.com or subject-specific equivalents. For instance, LogMap \cite{jimenez2011} leverages the UMLS lexicon to expand synonyms. This category also encompasses language models like BERTMap~\cite{he2022}, which undergo pre-training on large amounts of external textual content.

