\begin{proof}
    Define $\mathbf{V}_{c_2/c_1} := \{x\in \mathbb{R}^n:\, c_1 \le V_P(x)\le c_2\}$. If \eqref{eq:dVP} is satisfied, then all solutions $\varphi_x(k)$ of (\ref{eq:System}) starting in $\mathbf{V}_{c_2/c_1}$ cannot leave $\mathbf{V}_{c_2/c_1}$ until entering  $\mathbf{V}_{c_1}$ in finite time. By  Proposition \ref{prop:local_quad}, if a solution starts in or enters $\mathbf{V}_{c_1}$, it remains in $\mathbf{V}_{c_1}$ 
