    \noindent\textbf{Case 6: $H$ has exactly one bad twin group $B$, and $H[B]$ is independent set. Moreover, $B\subseteq U_- \sqcup U_+$ and $B\cap U_- \ne \emptyset$.} This corresponds to scenario b) of Statement 2 of Theorem \ref{thm:inducedchar}.

