\noindent \textbf{Reduction.}
%Reduction是BConv和PBS的最本质的运算，具有超过95%的运算量。Reduction类似于加法树的构造，我们在PE内如图3的数据流完成局部数据的乘累加，此时位于加法树的叶子节点的计算流程，接下来不断地往加法树的节点间计算，层层递归，即进行PE间的数据乘累加，但是我们只有一套PE，在树的不同层次时分复用地完成加法树的每一层计算。
Reduction is the core computation in BConv and PBS, accounting for more than $95\%$ of the total computation. In FlexMem, the overall reduction resembles an adder tree process. Each PE follows the ACC path in Fig.~\ref{fig:PE Core}, to complete the local reduction which corresponds to the computation at the leaf nodes of the adder tree. Subsequently, PE forwards partial results to other PEs within subarray pairs, where each PE corresponds to a node in the adder tree.
% Each node performs reduction with its sibling nodes, and the results serve as the parent node.
The reduction proceeds iteratively until all coefficients are reduced, with coefficients being transferred through the PE-chain. Since all RNS channels in RLWE and all LWE ciphertexts in TFHE PBS are allocated within the same subarray, the reduction does not require additional inter-subarray or inter-bank data exchange. 


%讲述根据变化多项式数量，动态数据重排
\subsection{Polynomial-level dataflow tuning}\label{sec:polynomial-level dataflow tuning}
%数据在线排布：我们数据排布方式难以一直保持高硬件利用率，我们基于对算法的观察，基于对硬件设计的利用，基于同态算法的静态性，提出重排布的方法，提高整体的硬件利用率，达到高吞吐
%问题观察，为什么要动态的排布，多项式并行度变化频繁
We propose a data remapping method based on the key observation that FlexMem suffers from performance degradation because of the frequent changes in polynomial-level parallelism, leading to low near-memory bandwidth utilization. 
%重排布如何使用以及在算法中发挥的作用
Remapping can change the number of columns for polynomial tiles in a subarray, i.e., $\#poly\_col$. For operators that change the number of polynomials, such as BConv, we remap either before the operator, reducing $\#poly\_col$ to allocate more columns for subsequently added polynomials, or after the operator that discards polynomials, thereby increasing $\#poly\_col$ to fill more coefficients in a subarray row. With remapping integrated into the computation flow, we adaptively adjust the polynomial-level dataflow, maintaining near-full utilization of the bandwidth. 

%重排的具体实现以及额外开销，操作可以简单地得到实现，并且极大的提高整体的性能，只有很小的额外开销
Remapping is conducted primarily through PE chains. Each remapping either doubles or halves the $\#poly\_col$. For example, as illustrated in Fig.~\ref{fig:remapping}, to expand the number of columns, the lower half of rows in a subarray are activated, starting from the bottom row in a pipelining manner. The data is then read into computational units, shifted rightward, and written back to the subarray. We show that the remapping is highly efficient in CKKS applications, which accounts for merely $0.68\%$ of the latency, significantly boosting bandwidth utilization and leading to $2.00\times$ of performance improvement in bootstrapping. 

