\subsection{Ciphertext-level dataflow design}\label{sec:ciphertext-level dataflow design}
%这章简单说，我们如何将运算负载分配到多个chip上。先从TFHE的PBS开始，一个chip即可完成多个密文的PBS，所有的bank分布式地存储bsk，共同完成一个ciphertext的PBS。CKKS 密文分散到两个chip keyswitch产生两个密文多项式的result，我们在一对chip中并行进行。对于CKKS的深层应用我们使用多个chip，如resnet或者boot的卷积操作，需要对密文进行不同步数的旋转操作之后乘以明文并求和，因此我们将密文clone多份，distribute到多个chip pair中，每个chip pair完成若干个密文rotation，在chip内进行局部的reduction，最终将各个chip的计算结果gather并求和。在这个过程中，我们通过chip-level的拓扑进行密文的distribute和collect，基于我们的互联设计，chip内的计算可以和transfer同时进行，使得流水线中掩盖了大部分的chip间搬运的时延
We further elaborate on the dataflow of high-level FHE operations. For TFHE, PBS for multiple ciphertexts can either be executed serially within a single chip to enhance data reuse or distributed across multiple chips in parallel for high throughput. 

%workload本身分配到多个 chip pair中，keyswitch分配到一个chip pair中
For CKKS, the core operator key switching is inherent parallel across two ciphertext polynomials and, therefore, allocated to a pair of chips. Higher-level applications that are built on key switching, are distributed across multiple chip pairs. 
%我们如何分配密文，确保chip pair的利用率
% Our design provides chip level scalability due to the general chip-level topology. 
We allocate an appropriate number of chips based on the ciphertext-level parallelism for a given task. 
%举个例子，boot，我们用多少个chip pair
For example, in bootstrapping with ARK~\cite{ARK} parameters, each baby-step computation involves eight parallel ciphertext rotations, which are allocated into four chip pairs, each handling two ciphertext rotations. 
%介绍distribution和collection怎么做的
Ciphertext-level communication patterns primarily consist of distribution and collection. The distribution phase begins with the first chip pair, where ciphertext-level computation is performed while simultaneously forwarding the input ciphertext to the next chip pair. Each chip pair starts its computation upon receiving the input ciphertext while forwarding it to the next pair. This continues until the last chip pair completes its task. In the collection phase, each pair first performs intra-chip reduction, then iteratively reduces results with its neighboring pair until the final reduction is completed. 


